## Why This Is Asked

Tests DP formulation for selecting fixed-count non-overlapping subarrays with a per-block cost, plus reconstruction of blocks.

## Key Concepts

- DP over i (prefix) and t (blocks)
- Prefix sums for subarray sums
- Running best to avoid O(n^2)
- Reconstructing start/end indices

## Code Example

```javascript
function maxKSubarraysWithCost(A, k, c){
  const n = A.length;
  const pref = new Array(n+1).fill(0);
  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) pref[i+1] = pref[i] + A[i];
  const NEG = -1e15;
  const dp = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => new Array(k+1).fill(NEG));
  const from = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => new Array(k+1).fill(null));
  dp[0][0] = 0;
  const bestVal = new Array(k+1).fill(NEG);
  const bestIdx = new Array(k+1).fill(-1);
  for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++){
    for (let t = 0; t <= k; t++){
      dp[i][t] = dp[i-1][t];
      from[i][t] = {type:'skip', at:i-1, t};
    }
    for (let t = 1; t <= k; t++){
      const val = dp[i-1][t-1] - pref[i-1];
      if (val > bestVal[t]) { bestVal[t] = val; bestIdx[t] = i-1; }
      const cand = bestVal[t] + pref[i] - c;
      if (cand > dp[i][t]) {
        dp[i][t] = cand;
        from[i][t] = {type:'end', end:i-1, start:bestIdx[t], t};
      }
    }
  }
  let i = n, t = k;
  const blocks = [];
  while (i > 0 && t > 0){
    const info = from[i][t];
    if (!info) break;
    if (info.type === 'end'){
      blocks.push([info.start, info.end]);
      i = info.start;
      t--;
    } else {
      i = info.at;
    }
  }
  blocks.reverse();
  return { value: dp[n][k], blocks };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you adapt for at-most-k blocks?
- How would you handle negative values of c or allow zero-cost blocks?
- What modifications optimize space to O(k) while preserving reconstruction?

## Why This Is Asked
Explores a new DP angle: subarray-level min as value, exact k non-overlapping blocks, with clear reconstruction.

## Key Concepts
- Partition DP with exact block count
- Precomputation of subarray minima
- Backtracking to obtain endpoints

## Code Example
```javascript
// Assumes A is 1-indexed, n = A.length-1, k given
function maxSumMinSubarrays(A, n, k) {
  const M = Array.from({length: n+2}, ()=>Array(n+2).fill(0));
  for (let l=1; l<=n; l++) {
    let m = A[l];
    for (let r=l; r<=n; r++) {
      m = Math.min(m, A[r]);
      M[l][r] = m;
    }
  }
  const dp = Array.from({length: n+1}, ()=>Array(k+1).fill(-Infinity));
  const opt = Array.from({length: n+1}, ()=>Array(k+1).fill(-1));
  dp[0][0] = 0;
  for (let i=1; i<=n; i++) {
    for (let t=1; t<=k; t++) {
      for (let l=1; l<=i; l++) {
        const cand = dp[l-1][t-1] + M[l][i];
        if (cand > dp[i][t]) { dp[i][t] = cand; opt[i][t] = l; }
      }
    }
  }
  // backtrack for endpoints
  let i = n, t = k, blocks = [];
  while (t > 0) {
    const l = opt[i][t];
    blocks.push([l, i]);
    i = l-1; t--;
  }
  blocks.reverse();
  return {sum: dp[n][k], blocks};
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests constrained path DP with an extra state (turns). Encourages explicit DP state design, directional transitions, and plan for path reconstruction.

## Key Concepts
- Grid DP with 4D state (i, j, t, dir)
- Transition logic depends on last direction
- Reconstruction via parent pointers
- Edge cases when k is large vs. maximum turns (n+m-2)

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxPathWithTurns(grid, k){
  const n = grid.length, m = grid[0].length;
  const NEG = -1e15;
  const dp = Array.from({length:n}, ()=>
    Array.from({length:m}, ()=>
      Array.from({length:k+1}, ()=> Array(2).fill(NEG))))
  dp[0][0][0][0] = grid[0][0];
  dp[0][0][0][1] = grid[0][0];
  for(let i=0;i<n;i++){
    for(let j=0;j<m;j++){
      for(let t=0;t<=k;t++){
        for(let dir=0;dir<2;dir++){
          const cur = dp[i][j][t][dir];
          if(cur===NEG) continue;
          // move right
          if(j+1<m){
            const nt = t + (dir===0?0:1);
            if(nt<=k) dp[i][j+1][nt][0] = Math.max(dp[i][j+1][nt][0], cur + grid[i][j+1]);
          }
          // move down
          if(i+1<n){
            const nt = t + (dir===1?0:1);
            if(nt<=k) dp[i+1][j][nt][1] = Math.max(dp[i+1][j][nt][1], cur + grid[i+1][j]);
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
  let ans = NEG;
  for(let t=0;t<=k;t++){
    ans = Math.max(ans, dp[n-1][m-1][t][0], dp[n-1][m-1][t][1]);
  }
  return ans;
}
```

